.TH WAVE-SELFUPDATE 1 "" "LinuxWave" "LinuxWave Manual"

.SH NAME
wave-selfupdate \- Update LinuxWave itself to the version published in the self-update repository.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wave selfupdate [flags]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Update LinuxWave itself to the version published in the self-update
repository.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-max\-time <string>
Maximum total time for one request (40s, 1min, 1min20s, 2h; a bare
number means seconds)
.TP
.B \-\-connect\-timeout <string>
Maximum time for the handshake
.TP
.B \-\-content\-time <string>
Maximum time to receive data
.TP
.B \-\-install\-python\-from\-source
Fetch the bundled Python from its upstream URL instead of LinuxWave's
own repository
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print what would be updated and change nothing (no download, no
agreement prompt)

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
wave selfupdate
wave selfupdate --max-time=2min
wave selfupdate --dry-run
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
wave(1)
